[gd_scene load_steps=12 format=3]

; ─────────────────────────────────────────────
; POLARIS — THE GAMEPLAY LAYER, AS ITS OWN SCENE.
;
; Same split as Georgetown and for the same reason: maps/polaris_level.tscn is
; written from a template by tools/build_polaris.gd, so anything hand-added to
; it dies on the next --force rebuild. tools/mission_ops.sh puts this back in
; two lines.
;
; Every position here was snapped to the baked navmesh and walked to from the
; spawn by tools/probe_mission_anchors.gd before it was written down.
;
; ── WHAT THIS MAP IS FOR ─────────────────────
; A WAVE DEFENCE, and it is the only map in the project shaped for one.
;
; The reason is the ring road. It is a CLOSED loop round the mall with four
; arterial approaches into it — the frontage to the south, Sancus Boulevard to
; the west, the subdivision street to the north, the basin side to the east —
; and no corner of the site a vehicle cannot reach. On every other map the
; opposition arrives along an axis. Here it can arrive from any of four, and
; keep arriving.
;
; THE GROUND YOU HOLD is the mall's entry court. It is not a fort and that is
; the point: the mall is at your back with no way through it, the cinema looks
; into the court from the west and the parking deck from the east, and in front
; of it is four hundred metres of car park whose only cover is parked cars at
; 1.45 m — over the 1.2 m a standing cover point probes at and under a head, so
; a row of them is cover you fire over from a crouch and get shot over from a
; stand. The aisles and their islands run north-south, which means they are
; cover for whoever is crossing and not for whoever is holding.
;
; So the court is defensible in one direction and open in three, and holding it
; is about who you send where rather than about standing in the right spot.
;
; ── HOW THE WAVES ARE BUILT ──────────────────
; With nothing new. A reserve's `reinforcement_tag` IS an objective id, so:
;
;   pol_breach completes  ->  spawner.wake("pol_breach")   ->  wave 1 arrives
;   pol_wave_1 completes  ->  spawner.wake("pol_wave_1")   ->  wave 2 arrives
;   ...and so on to wave 5.
;
; Each wave's objective carries `starts_active = false` and the PREVIOUS wave
; as its prerequisite, so it activates on exactly the frame its own squads are
; built. That matters twice: EliminateObjective pushes a warning when it has
; been active for six seconds with no targets found, and the objective HUD
; would otherwise show all five waves from the first minute and give the whole
; shape away.
;
; `required_kills` on each wave is deliberately BELOW the wave's body count.
; The classic wave-defence stall is one surviving chaser hiding behind the
; garden centre while the player hunts the map for it; two or three bodies of
; slack means the wave ends when the wave is broken.
; ─────────────────────────────────────────────

